00:35:35,136 --> 00:35:36,872
I was just heading to
the briefing room.

474
00:35:36,907 --> 00:35:38,852
You got no call to be in there,
so flee.

475
00:35:38,865 --> 00:35:41,733
Lieutenant, this fucking
guy doesn't belong.

476
00:35:41,766 --> 00:35:43,393
I'm still waiting for
his spatter report

477
00:35:43,405 --> 00:35:46,331
on the cokehead murders --
Go do that.

478
00:35:46,367 --> 00:35:48,562
It's okay.
I don't want to upset anybody.

479
00:35:48,605 --> 00:35:51,553
He can stay.
I'd like your input,

480
00:35:51,576 --> 00:35:54,111
and we'll discuss your
case after the meeting.

481
00:35:55,238 --> 00:35:56,700
How about we get started?

482
00:35:56,727 --> 00:35:59,572
- ¿Encontráste algo?
- Nada todavía.

483
00:35:59,608 --> 00:36:02,012
- Hazme un favor y quítate la gorra.
- Discúlpame.

484
00:36:10,738 --> 00:36:14,602
- You ready?
- I'm gonna shame this bitch.

485
00:36:14,637 --> 00:36:17,781
Just state your case clean and easy.
You'll be the hero.

486
00:36:17,835 --> 00:36:20,931
Okay, settle down.

487
00:36:20,968 --> 00:36:23,501
Now, has anyone tracked
down that witness?

488
00:36:26,206 --> 00:36:29,762
Come on, people.
Someone needs to find something here.

489
00:36:29,908 --> 00:36:34,150
- Lieutenant Laguerta?
- Officer Morgan.

490
00:36:34,206 --> 00:36:36,352
I didn't recognize you
with your clothes on.

491
00:36:38,408 --> 00:36:42,962
I have an idea,
something in a different direction.

492
00:36:43,507 --> 00:36:44,962
An idea?

493
00:36:46,765 --> 00:36:48,741
Well, please, share it with us.

494
00:36:53,117 --> 00:36:56,571
- Cell crystallization.
- Excuse me?

495
00:36:56,607 --> 00:36:59,123
A little more confidence,
please.

496
00:37:01,166 --> 00:37:02,302
On the last victim,

497
00:37:02,335 --> 00:37:04,772
I'd like to check and see
if any refrigerated trucks

498
00:37:04,806 --> 00:37:09,681
have been stolen in
the last... week or so.

499
00:37:10,206 --> 00:37:13,522
Refrigerated trucks
like ice-cream trucks?

500
00:37:14,635 --> 00:37:19,831
No, not ice-cream trucks.

501
00:37:19,866 --> 00:37:21,330
A refrigerated vehicle

502
00:37:21,367 --> 00:37:23,833
that could cause that
kind of tissue damage,

503
00:37:23,868 --> 00:37:26,652
a refrigerated truck that's...

504
00:37:26,766 --> 00:37:30,060
...mobile so he'll be
harder to catch,

505
00:37:30,137 --> 00:37:35,431
a refrigerated truck that
might give us a lead.

506
00:37:38,598 --> 00:37:41,452
That's very interesting,
very creative.

507
00:37:41,478 --> 00:37:43,182
Let's keep looking
for the witness, okay?

508
00:37:43,196 --> 00:37:45,502
We know that he or she is out there.
The forensic evidence,

509
00:37:45,638 --> 00:37:47,672
the interrupted cut proves
that there was an eyewitness.

510
00:37:47,706 --> 00:37:50,162
Now, somebody out
there saw something,

511
00:37:50,205 --> 00:37:52,712
so let's concentrate on
finding that person, okay?

512
00:37:52,737 --> 00:37:53,361
But --

513
00:37:53,387 --> 00:37:56,113
Just keep talking
to all your hookers.

514
00:37:57,607 --> 00:38:00,100
That's all for today.

515
00:38:06,637 --> 00:38:10,411
What the fuck was I supposed to say?
The only reason I'm in here

516
00:38:10,536 --> 00:38:12,721
is because the captain said
they had to let me in.

517
00:38:12,807 --> 00:38:15,392
But he didn't say they
had to listen to you.

518
00:38:15,405 --> 00:38:16,801
Well, right again.

519
00:38:16,845 --> 00:38:19,731
So say adiós to my career.
I'm gonna die a meter maid.

520
00:38:19,766 --> 00:38:23,542
Stop it. Deb, there's another way.
Find the truck.

521
00:38:27,866 --> 00:38:32,330
Excuse me, Dexter...
My office, please.

522
00:38:39,467 --> 00:38:41,662
What the hell?

523
00:38:44,668 --> 00:38:47,160
What the fuck?

524
00:38:48,616 --> 00:38:51,203
Are you boning her?

525
00:38:51,228 --> 00:38:53,690
- No.
- Oh, my god!

526
00:38:53,736 --> 00:38:56,513
- Deb, wait.
- Shut up.

527
00:39:00,068 --> 00:39:01,800
It had nothing to
do with drugs.

528
00:39:01,837 --> 00:39:03,901
L.T., this is a waste
of our damn time.

529
00:39:03,936 --> 00:39:05,682
I think sergeant
Doakes is right.

530
00:39:05,708 --> 00:39:07,932
I read the other reports,
all the other forensic analysis.

531
00:39:07,965 --> 00:39:11,171
Everyone agrees the cokehead murders
had nothing to do with cocaine.

532
00:39:11,206 --> 00:39:12,933
It was a crime of passion.

533
00:39:12,968 --> 00:39:15,650
The murderer came to kill
the woman, not the dealer.

534
00:39:15,678 --> 00:39:17,003
He did him quick and
got him out of the way.

535
00:39:17,036 --> 00:39:19,570
But he sure as hell took his
sweet time slicing up that lady,

536
00:39:19,606 --> 00:39:22,003
and you don't do that
unless you have a close,

537
00:39:22,035 --> 00:39:26,750
personal relationship with someone.
Probably an ex-boyfriend.

538
00:39:26,835 --> 00:39:28,903
That's who I'd look for.

539
00:39:31,655 --> 00:39:33,083
Okay.

540
00:39:33,306 --> 00:39:37,492
It's a bit of a push, but,
sergeant, you should check it out.

541
00:39:45,268 --> 00:39:48,200
I'm watching you, motherfucker.

542
00:40:01,537 --> 00:40:03,962
<i>Jaworski's been coming
here for weeks --</i>

543
00:40:04,007 --> 00:40:06,563
<i>likes to steal all
the copper plumbing.</i>

544
00:40:06,605 --> 00:40:09,091
<i>There's good money in that.</i>

545
00:40:09,906 --> 00:40:13,402
<i>No security guards --
that's good.</i>

546
00:41:17,568 --> 00:41:19,580
- Fuck!
- Talk.

547
00:41:19,597 --> 00:41:22,381
- What do you mean?
- I think you know what I mean.

548
00:41:22,407 --> 00:41:26,010
No. Oh, god.

549
00:41:26,036 --> 00:41:28,852
Talk to me about Jane Saunders.

550
00:41:29,468 --> 00:41:31,932
Okay.
I did her.

551
00:41:31,968 --> 00:41:35,612
- How?
- In a movie -- snuff film.

552
00:41:35,636 --> 00:41:39,330
- But I'm not sorry.
- Of course not.

553
00:41:40,506 --> 00:41:43,400
No, I'm not sorry, either.

554
00:42:05,306 --> 00:42:10,962
- Hello?
- Hey. I'm -- I'm sorry.

555
00:42:11,006 --> 00:42:14,132
I mean,
I'm sorry about the other night,

556
00:42:14,166 --> 00:42:20,013
but... look, Dex, I really,
really need to see you.

557
00:42:20,166 --> 00:42:24,932
So can you --
can you come by later,

558
00:42:24,965 --> 00:42:27,262
you know, just for,
like, a little while?

559
00:42:27,306 --> 00:42:29,702
I mean, I'm really --

560
00:42:31,067 --> 00:42:34,132
All right.
What are you doing now?

561
00:42:34,567 --> 00:42:36,460
I'm just finishing
up a little project,

562
00:42:36,505 --> 00:42:38,913
but I'll come by later.

563
00:42:38,918 --> 00:42:41,192
Okay, bye.

564
00:42:56,136 --> 00:42:58,533
<i>All in all,
it was a good night.</i>

565
00:42:58,768 --> 00:43:02,432
<i>One less amateur filmmaker
polluting the internet.</i>

566
00:43:34,038 --> 00:43:36,071
No way !

567
00:45:11,567 --> 00:45:13,802
Give us a minute.

568
00:45:14,338 --> 00:45:16,863
Hanging in there?

569
00:45:17,067 --> 00:45:19,710
This will teach me to tailgate.

570
00:45:19,858 --> 00:45:21,702
Let's go over this again.

571
00:45:21,738 --> 00:45:25,602
- I'm all yours.
- So all the ice trucks in Miami --

572
00:45:26,038 --> 00:45:29,732
- bit of a coincidence, don't you think?
- Sure, during business hours.

573
00:45:29,907 --> 00:45:32,402
But this time of night,
a truck like that sticks out.

574
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:34,300
And you followed it.

575
00:45:35,526 --> 00:45:36,952
That's right.

576
00:45:36,965 --> 00:45:41,282
- You never saw the driver?
- Just high beams and a flying head.

577
00:45:41,938 --> 00:45:46,000
So then he must have already had
the head with him in the front seat.

578
00:45:46,307 --> 00:45:49,331
That's weird.
Why would he keep it there?

579
00:45:49,366 --> 00:45:51,930
I don't know,
so he could use a carpool lane?

580
00:45:55,805 --> 00:45:59,602
It just seems odd.
Your sister has this ice-truck theory,

581
00:45:59,706 --> 00:46:02,301
and then here you
are to back it up.

582
00:46:02,336 --> 00:46:05,230
She's good, lieutenant.
You should give her a chance.

583
00:46:05,565 --> 00:46:08,633
You know,
you should call me Maria.

584
00:46:08,716 --> 00:46:12,100
But I'll tell you who's good --
you are.

585
00:46:12,136 --> 00:46:15,163
Doakes picked up the killer
in the cokehead murders.

586
00:46:15,406 --> 00:46:18,242
You were right.
It was her boyfriend.

587
00:46:18,448 --> 00:46:21,052
Of course, Doakes
still hates you.

588
00:46:21,427 --> 00:46:22,951
Of course.

589
00:46:26,037 --> 00:46:28,611
Tell me, Dexter,

590
00:46:28,647 --> 00:46:31,203
how did you get
to be so smart?

591
00:46:33,807 --> 00:46:36,481
Lots of sleep.

592
00:46:39,606 --> 00:46:41,851
Is it okay if I fill out
that report tomorrow?

593
00:46:43,468 --> 00:46:46,530
Sure thing.
You're tired.

594
00:46:48,068 --> 00:46:52,562
- Good night, lieutenant.
- I'll catch you later.

595
00:47:07,067 --> 00:47:11,113
Dex.
It's been a while.

596
00:47:11,167 --> 00:47:15,131
- I'm sorry.
- I was worried.

597
00:47:15,167 --> 00:47:18,361
I didn't know what to do.
I called in sick.

598
00:47:19,037 --> 00:47:21,161
I mean...

599
00:47:23,807 --> 00:47:27,081
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine. I was just --

600
00:47:27,465 --> 00:47:30,832
I'm sorry.
There was another... You know.

601
00:47:39,305 --> 00:47:43,400
Look... The kids
slept over next door.

602
00:47:44,487 --> 00:47:46,462
Okay.

603
00:47:47,328 --> 00:47:52,232
- Would you like to come in?
- Okay.

604
00:47:52,268 --> 00:47:54,231
Okay.

605
00:48:06,837 --> 00:48:09,531
I don't want to lose you, Dex.

606
00:48:11,335 --> 00:48:14,102
Okay, sure.

607
00:48:16,166 --> 00:48:22,332
And... well... I want you.

608
00:48:22,865 --> 00:48:24,531
I mean...

609
00:48:33,667 --> 00:48:37,233
Okay.
Thanks.

610
00:48:38,917 --> 00:48:41,201
You're welcome.

611
00:49:01,168 --> 00:49:05,533
- Do you mind?
- No.

612
00:49:19,807 --> 00:49:24,590
- It could be the kids.
- Better get it, then.

613
00:49:28,638 --> 00:49:31,030
Hello?

614
00:49:31,407 --> 00:49:33,432
Cody.

615
00:49:33,468 --> 00:49:35,260
Cody, stop crying, sweetie.

616
00:49:37,866 --> 00:49:41,363
All right.
I'll come get you.

617
00:49:44,168 --> 00:49:48,263
Cody just threw up all
over Colleen's couch.

618
00:49:49,668 --> 00:49:52,502
I got to go get him.

619
00:49:56,868 --> 00:50:01,920
- Tell me we're okay.
- Better than.

620
00:50:02,777 --> 00:50:06,930
- Okay.
- Go be a good mom.

621
00:50:25,535 --> 00:50:27,903
<i>Okay, that was close.</i>

622
00:50:30,337 --> 00:50:33,600
<i>I'll admit,
making out with Rita was...</i>

623
00:50:33,638 --> 00:50:35,902
<i>Interesting.</i>

624
00:50:36,147 --> 00:50:37,990
<i>But if I don't keep a lid on this,</i>

625
00:50:38,006 --> 00:50:39,692
<i>it could be the end of us.</i>

626
00:51:02,905 --> 00:51:07,412
<i>I suppose I should be upset,
even feel violated,</i>

627
00:51:07,587 --> 00:51:09,841
<i>but I'm not.</i>

628
00:51:10,145 --> 00:51:12,523
<i>No.</i>

629
00:51:12,556 --> 00:51:14,280
<i>In fact,
I think this is a friendly message,</i>

630
00:51:14,308 --> 00:51:17,730
<i>kind of like,
"hey, want to play?"</i>

631
00:51:18,438 --> 00:51:21,732
<i>And, yes, I want to play.</i>

632
00:51:21,966 --> 00:51:24,042
<i>I really, really do.</i>

633
00:51:27,166 --> 00:51:33,211
Synchro: Travis
Transcript: Raceman
